## Report: dramafinder 1.1.6 + Playwright API for Vaadin/Spring Boot test

No `-sources.jar` exists in the repo (only jar + pom), so API below is from `javap` on the jar itself.

### Base test class
`org.vaadin.addons.dramafinder.AbstractBasePlaywrightIT` (implements `HasTestView`):
```java
protected Page page;                       // available in subclass
public void setupTest() throws Exception;   // @BeforeEach-annotated internally; creates page, navigates
public void cleanupTest();                  // closes page
protected Page getPage();
protected Browser getBrowser();
protected Playwright getPlaywright();
protected static boolean isHeadless();
```
`HasTestView`:
```java
public abstract String getUrl();   // e.g. return "http://localhost:" + port + "/route"
public default String getView();
```
Extend `AbstractBasePlaywrightIT`, implement `getUrl()` returning `"http://localhost:" + port + yourRoute` where `port` comes from `@LocalServerPort` in a `@SpringBootTest(webEnvironment = RANDOM_PORT)` test class (the jar has no Spring integration itself — you provide the URL).

### Locating Vaadin components — no CSS selectors needed
Every element type has a static `getByLabel(Page, String)` / `getByLabel(Locator, String)` (or `getByText`/`getById` for some), backed by `AccessibleNameLocator.find(Page, String, AriaRole, String)`, which does an accessible-name/role lookup:
```java
TextFieldElement name = TextFieldElement.getByLabel(page, "Name");
MultiSelectComboBoxElement tags = MultiSelectComboBoxElement.getByLabel(page, "Tags");
GridElement grid = GridElement.get(page);              // or GridElement.getById(page, "my-grid")
ButtonElement save = ButtonElement.getByText(page, "Save");
```
Common `HasValueElement` (implemented by TextField/ComboBox/MultiSelectComboBox etc.):
```java
String getValue();
void setValue(String);   // internally: inputLocator.fill(value); dispatchEvent("change"); waitForVaadinIdle()
void clear();
void assertValue(String);
```
Note: `setValue` uses `Locator.fill()` — a single DOM value set + one change event, NOT per-keystroke. For a "no request per keystroke" test, bypass this and drive the raw Playwright locator directly with `pressSequentially`, e.g. `nameField.getInputLocator().pressSequentially("abc", new Locator.PressSequentiallyOptions().setDelay(50))`.

`MultiSelectComboBoxElement` key methods: `open()/close()/isOpened()`, `selectItem(String)`, `selectItems(String...)`, `filterAndSelectItem(filter, item)`, `getSelectedItems()`, `getSelectedItemCount()`, `assertSelectedItems(String...)`.

`GridElement`: `getRenderedRowCount()`, `getTotalRowCount()`, `findRow(int)` → `RowElement` (`getCell(int|String)` → `CellElement`), `findCell(int,String)`, `findHeaderCellByText(String)`, `select(int)`, `assertRowCount(int)`, `assertCellContent(row, col, text)`.

### Playwright wiring (offline)
```java
Playwright pw = Playwright.create();
Browser browser = pw.chromium().launch(new BrowserType.LaunchOptions().setHeadless(true));
Page page = browser.newPage();
page.navigate("http://localhost:" + port + "/my-route");
```
`AbstractBasePlaywrightIT` already does this via `ThreadLocal<Playwright>`/`ThreadLocal<Browser>` static fields and `setupTest()`; just implement `getUrl()`.

### Current URL
`Page.url()` → `public abstract String url();`

### Counting network requests
```java
List<Request> seen = new ArrayList<>();
page.onRequest(req -> seen.add(req));      // or filter req.url().contains("?v-r=") for Vaadin XHR
// ... perform interaction ...
page.offRequest(listener);                  // to detach
int count = seen.size();
```
Also available: `onResponse(Consumer<Response>)`/`offResponse`, `onRequestFinished`, `waitForRequest(String|Pattern|Predicate, Runnable)`, `waitForResponse(...)`. For asserting "typing doesn't fire per keystroke," register `onRequest` before typing, type via `pressSequentially`, then assert `seen.size()` stays 0 (or 1, post-debounce) rather than equal to keystroke count.

### Browser binaries offline
`/root/.cache/ms-playwright` already contains `chromium-1217`, `chromium_headless_shell-1217`, `firefox-1511`, `webkit-2272`, `ffmpeg-1011`. `HOME=/root`, and Playwright's Java driver defaults to `~/.cache/ms-playwright` on Linux when `PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH` is unset — confirmed unset in this env, so **no env var is needed**; `pw.chromium().launch(...)` will resolve chromium-1217 automatically.

Maven coords already resolved: `com.microsoft.playwright:playwright:1.59.0` plus `driver`/`driver-bundle:1.59.0` (transitive, no npm/network fetch required).

